course: dictionary
lesson: 15460
title: Formal words in rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound stiff and formal, and you often find them in rules, agreements and contracts. «Stipulate» is one of them. It is a verb, and it means to state clearly that something must be done.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. «The rules stipulate that answers must be in pen.» The word «must» tells you the rule is firm. Stipulate means the rules say clearly that answers have to be in pen, so pencil is not allowed.
explain: Maths and exam papers often use this voice. «It is stipulated that each box holds 12.» That means each box must hold 12, so you can use 12 in your sum. Everyday words that mean nearly the same are say clearly, require and insist.
fact: «Stipulate» is a verb, so it has forms such as stipulates, stipulated and stipulating.
fact: «Stipulate» means to state clearly that something must be done.
fact: You often find «stipulate» in rules, agreements and contracts.
fact: «The rules stipulate that answers must be in pen.» means the rules clearly say answers must be in pen.
fact: Everyday words for «stipulate» include say clearly, require and insist.
exercise: «The rules stipulate that answers must be in pen.» What does stipulate mean here? | Draw a picture to help | Rub out a mistake | Guess at a sum | *Say clearly that something must be done
exercise: «It is stipulated that each box holds 12.» In this sentence, what must happen? | *Each box has to hold 12 | Each box might hold about 5 | Each box can hold anything | Boxes are not counted
exercise: Which everyday word is closest in meaning to stipulate? | Forget | Giggle | *Require | Wobble
test: «The contract stipulates that the rent is paid on the first day of each month.» What does the contract say? | The rent may be paid whenever you like | The rent is paid on a Sunday only | The rent is never paid | *The rent must be paid on the first day of each month
test: Which word is the best everyday replacement for «stipulate» in «The club stipulates that members must pay each year»? | *Insist | Dance | Vanish | Whisper
exam: The sign stipulates that dogs must be kept on a lead. What does the sign say? | Dogs are welcome to sing | Dogs should wear hats | *Dogs must be kept on a lead | Dogs can run free in the park
